# Awayra Project Rules

- Build a Windows-only WPF application using .NET 10 LTS
- Use MVVM with CommunityToolkit.Mvvm
- Keep business logic in `Awayra.Core` without WPF references
- Use `System.Windows.Forms.NotifyIcon` for the tray
- Persist data locally with `System.Text.Json` under `%LocalAppData%\Awayra\`
- No preview SDKs, no Electron/Tauri/Rust/Node/web stacks
- Run focused tests during development; full suite at milestones
- Debug via `scripts/dev.ps1`; publish via `scripts/publish.ps1` only after tests pass
- Run `scripts/verify-change.ps1` before declaring any task complete
- No installer unless explicitly requested
- No Git push
- Never modify tests to hide defects
- Never touch `D:\curser\AWAYRA\AWAYRA`

## Required change workflow

1. Inspect scope and list allowed files
2. Record protected behaviors from `docs/CHANGE_GUARD.md`
3. Baseline tests before editing
4. Smallest possible patch only
5. Inspect `git diff` after editing
6. Run focused tests, then `scripts/verify-change.ps1`
7. Never mix UI changes with backend fixes, or behavior changes with styling fixes
8. Never commit or push unless explicitly requested
9. Task is **BLOCKED** if regression verification fails
